{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > collab/yang-clojure/1794729000000-engineer-d1-r10-declaration-tagged-run.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md <<'EOF'\n# D1 r10 — bounds and verification continuation\n\nStatus: **in progress; no complete declaration or bounded verification result**. Worktree mirror, no commit; the r9e store is \"'`target/d1-r9e-retained-store` and remains uncommitted with retention location/owner pending. The r9g explicit sequencing resolution authorizes pre-declaration pilots, with only a later declaration-governed run counting as verification.\n\n## Trace memory pilot\n\nA scratch JVM `java.lang.instrument.Instrumentation` agent in `target/CorrespondenceSizeAgent.java` (SHA-256 `aa3b55e12582fcd419cb06eb30066ee4d5e04c32a83dc0b4f7ee7053e1adb170`) measures the sum of JVM shallow sizes over the identity-deduplicated graph reachable from each halted ring trace handle. It traverses object reference fields and arrays, refuses inaccessible fields, counts shared reachable objects, and is not exclusive retained size, native memory or a portable VM layout. The command uses the JDK module opens recorded in `target/d1-r10-trace-memory.clj` invocation logs. The two-slot shared-object probe failed to compile before agent creation, then passed with the agent. This is local scratch instrumentation, not a published verification dependency.\n\n`1794729000000-engineer-d1-r10-trace-memory.edn` (SHA-256 `42e60986b3ef0fbf4f8574aa678ff75ed12b214cc45a911a8901dc8b9d6431e7`) records **155 pilot passes**, both lanes and no detected prefix loss, all pre-declaration. Each per-lane record includes max individual printed-record UTF-8 bytes and graph size, plus steps, total printed trace bytes and times. The per-lane maximum reachable ring graph is 311,144 bytes and maximum individual printed record 45 bytes. This is an observed maximum for these runs, not proof that an arbitrary 1,000,000-record ring consumes only that much; serialised vector bytes are not ring memory or a byte-capacity enforcement mechanism. The batch heap sampler'\"'s process-wide peak was 3,589,539,800 bytes at 5 ms; the agent graph walk adds work, and its measurement time is included in the reported drain phase. Logs: \"'`target/d1-r10-trace-memory-01.log` and `-02.log`.\n\n## Enforcement and baseline work\n\n`test/yang/correspondence_lane.clj` now reports max printed-record bytes and can invoke an explicit per-step runtime check. `yang.correspondence-measure/runtime-checker` checks steps, monotonic elapsed time, observed process used heap and current ring record positions, refusing missing trace handles, evicted prefixes or a declared maximum exceeded. It checks at step boundaries, so it is a sampled used-heap limit, not an operating-system memory cap or a bound on a single host operation; a complete bounded driver still needs to wire it in and record all refusal evidence. Red-first tests cover a runtime cutoff and exceeded time, heap and record limits. A trace-free source preparation helper checks the entire captured oracle suffix, preserving the already-assembled library prefix and refusing assembly or collection-order/metadata fidelity mismatches; it does not invent a new retained origin. Its negative tests were observed red first.\n\nThe first trace-free baseline candidate for `:minimal-last` refused at `:baseline-assembly`; that refusal is preserved in `1794729000000-engineer-d1-r10-baseline-pilot.edn`, not rewritten. A diagnostic intended to explain the mismatch first failed due to a two-argument `jing/get` call; `target/d1-r10-baseline-diagnose-02.log` is the corrected, currently-running diagnostic. Even a successful trace-free run plus the test script'\"'s ephemeral application-path index would not alone satisfy the full B/S comparison: C1/provenance production/persistence/loading/query, old two-field tracing, cold/warm workload repetitions and matched phase/delta measurements remain to be established. Do not call an ephemeral benchmark path a persisted C1 occurrence.\n\n## Remaining work\n\nNo complete finite bounds declaration was finalized; the r8/r9g draft and raw pilot observations remain available. Neither a bounded tagged verification run, full independent D1 recipe/record, image/derivation/provenance checks, companion nor separate verification result has been published. Trace byte capacity and real-time enforcement, full baseline and phase comparisons, a complete runtime driver and preservation of all exceeded-limit evidence remain open. The full oracle suite was not run. The current focused correspondence tests passed 13 tests / 50 assertions before any subsequent changes; final lint and verification must be recorded after edits.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
