{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,55p' src/cljc/yang/correspondence_text.clj; rg -n 'fixed-jvm|metadata|numeric' collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r5.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md | head\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.correspondence-text\n  \"JVM text capture pilot. Acceptance still requires a pinned dependency closure\n   and per-compilation replay of every claimed artifact.\"\n  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]))\n\n\n(def profile\n  {:yang.correspondence.text/schema 1\n   :host :jvm\n   :clojure-version (clojure-version)\n   :java-version (System/getProperty \"java.version\")\n   :java-vendor (System/getProperty \"java.vendor\")\n   :encoding :utf-8\n   :normalization :none\n   :printer 'clojure.core/pr-str\n   :printer-options {:meta true :length nil :level nil :readably true\n                     :dup false :namespace-maps false}\n   :reader 'clojure.edn/read\n   :reader-options {:values 1 :eof-required true :ambient-readers false\n                    :tags :unsupported}\n   :domain :edn-with-readable-metadata\n   :fidelity-rule :fixed-jvm-integer-wrappers-v1})\n\n\n(defn- kind\n  [x]\n  (cond (map? x) :map (vector? x) :vector (set? x) :set\n        (seq? x) :list (sequential? x) :sequence :else :scalar))\n\n\n(def ^:private fixed-integer-classes #{Byte Short Integer Long})\n\n\n(def ^:private supported-numeric-classes\n  #{Byte Short Integer Long clojure.lang.BigInt java.math.BigInteger\n    java.math.BigDecimal clojure.lang.Ratio Double Float})\n\n\n(defn- numeric-faithful?\n  [a b]\n  (and (number? a) (number? b)\n       (let [ca (class a) cb (class b)]\n         (cond\n           (and (contains? fixed-integer-classes ca)\n                (contains? fixed-integer-classes cb)) (= (long a) (long b))\n           (and (= ca cb) (contains? supported-numeric-classes ca)) (.equals a b)\n           :else false))))\n\n\n(defn- mismatch\n  [a b path]\n  (cond\n    (not= (kind a) (kind b)) {:path path :reason :kind :actual (kind a) :read (kind b)}\n    (not= (some? (meta a)) (some? (meta b))) {:path path :reason :metadata-presence}\n    :else\n7:`yang.correspondence-text/profile` now includes `:fidelity-rule :fixed-jvm-integer-wrappers-v1`, so its content address differs from the r4 class-strict profile. Its numeric comparison permits equal Byte/Short/Integer/Long values via exact `long` comparison; all other admitted numeric leaves require same class and `.equals` (including Double NaN, signed zero and BigDecimal scale). Numeric dispatch occurs before generic `=`. Tests cover all four wrapper pairs, changed numeric coordinates, missing metadata, Long/BigInt, decimal scale, signed zero, NaN, collection kind and map/set iteration order. This is scoped to this experimental JVM profile and does not establish behavior for arbitrary programs.\n9:The map mismatch path includes the map entry's actual key; capture failures name fixture, supplied admission scope, ordinal and input. The real-fixture test identifies r4's original mismatch precisely: `:beta-eq-false` forms `[15 2]` metadata entry 2 is `:line`, whose value is Integer before printing and Long after reading, with equal value. The amended capture **was observed to pass** on this fixture; it retains the supplied fresh admission coordinate and all four text captures. It does not change the historical r4 failure.\n13:For the one `:beta-eq-false` admission, the new test captures the original input, reads the captured text, recompiles, and compares its root, oracle canonical-source-hash, producer-derived site table, C1 metadata, site binding, stamped root/metadata and explicit stamped-to-unstamped correspondence with the original compilation. It validates both row trees and their application coverage; stamping adds two unmarked applications per wrapper, accounted separately from the C1 markers per the post-port cc3 test. It stores input, profile, expectations, and both canonical row closures in a file-backed store, closes and reopens it, checks all retained row bodies, and repeats the comparisons using fetched input/expectations. This runs only static compilation: no tagged machine, trace or verifier result. Test store is deleted after the test and is not durable publication of a corpus record.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
